#---
# purpose: "opaque call through a multi-clause function value whose selected clause depends on the argument's runtime type"
#---
#
# # opaque_fn_mixed_return
#
# `mapper`'s integer clause returns a value; its atom clause diverges through
# `panic`, so the published callable boundary carries one returning and one
# divergent member. `mapper` is passed as a value to `Enum.map`, which calls it
# opaquely. The taken path selects the integer clause and prints `2`.
def mapper(x :: integer), do: x + 1
def mapper(x :: atom), do: panic(x)

def main() do
  n = Process.heap_alloc_stats()[:allocs]
  x = case n < n + 1 do
    true -> 1
    _ -> :bad
  end
  [y] = Enum.map([x], mapper)
  dbg(y)
end
